  "construction_notes": [
    {
      "text": "Replaces an existing single-story five-unit residential building, so the net gain is 5 homes",
      "src": [
        "SRC-001017"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Plan set cover sheet: owner DNL Real Estate Development LLC; site area about 12,820 sq ft; zoning Mixed Use Medium II (General Plan 2040); 20 resident and 2 visitor parking spaces; demolition of three existing single-story residential buildings containing six units. The city page describes the existing building as a single-story five-unit residential building.",
      "src": [
        "SRC-004064",
        "SRC-001017"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Neighborhood meeting summary dates the meeting July 8, 2026, held on Zoom; the city page gives July 14, 2026. Applicant team at the meeting: Haonan Jia and Yidan Hu of Haonan Studio. The applicant described the units as three bedrooms plus an office; the city page describes each unit as 4 bedrooms.",
      "src": [
        "SRC-004063",
        "SRC-001017"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "An earlier planning application at this site, 'One Hayward', proposed a 4-story mixed-use building with ground-floor business space and 18 rental units (3 junior one-bedrooms, 15 one-bedrooms) over one level of subterranean parking, using the state density bonus with 16% very low income BMR units. Owner shown as One Hayward Avenue LLC (Redwood City); architect Arc Tec Inc.; civil engineer BKF Engineers; landscape architect JETT. Submittals ran from 2019-10-03 to resubmittal V on 2021-07-22. The 2026 neighborhood meeting summary refers to a 2021 approved apartment building at the site.",
      "src": [
        "SRC-004066",
        "SRC-004063"
      ]
    }
  ],
